  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Wash needs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PEF is a non-profit (non-governmental) association established in 1998. It provides important services in the environment and natural resources fields to all Palestinians without discrimination. PEF has a strong track record and long-term experience working in the WASH sector and successfully supports vulnerable communities throughout the Gaza Strip to access basic WASH services. PEF ensures equitable, affordable, and sustainable access to safe and sufficient WASH services protecting the dignity of the unserved, underserved and most vulnerable Palestinians living under occupation in the Gaza Strip. PEF has developed a strong capacity to implement WASH, engineering, and public health activities. PEF engineers and hygiene promotion teams were involved and consulted in the design andplanning of the proposed project and supported in coordinating with relevant authorities and municipalities.
Under this program, PEF will be responsible about the day-to-day implementation of activities under outcome 2, namelythe shelter on HHs and WASH on community level components.  PEF will prepare the tender documents including the BOQs and technical assessments of the targeted HHs. PEF will supervise and follow up the rehabilitation and maintenance works which will be undertaken by experienced private contractors, who will be selected through a competitive tendering process.</narrative>
  </description>
